---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { sorted } from '../lib/topics';
import TopicCard from '../components/TopicCard.astro';

const topics = sorted(await getCollection('topics'));
---
<Base title="WAGademy — protected time to get research done">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Commit · work · report</p>
      <h1>The thesis isn't writing itself.</h1>
      <p>
        WAGademy is a Working Accountability Group for HDR students, run in the Imaging, Sensing and
        Biomedical Engineering discipline at UQ: protected hours of focused work, alongside other
        people doing the same. Everything needed to run one — or to run it alone — is here.
      </p>
      <div class="btn-row">
        <a class="btn" href="/board/">Set your goals</a>
        <a class="btn ghost" style="border-color:var(--cream);color:var(--cream)" href="/timer/">Open the timer</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The method, in three steps</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Commit.</strong> Say your goals out loud, and put them somewhere visible.</li>
        <li><strong>Work.</strong> Three 50-minute pomodoros, phones away, alongside other people.</li>
        <li><strong>Report.</strong> Did you hit it? What got in the way? No judgment — it's data.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        That's the whole thing. It needs a room, a timer and three other people — and it works with
        no material at all. <a href="/about/">Why it works</a> is worth five minutes if you're not
        yet convinced; <a href="/run-your-own/">Run your own</a> is the run sheet if you are.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Two tools</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <a class="card" href="/board/">
        <span class="num">Before you start</span>
        <h3>Goal board</h3>
        <p>
          Write what you're doing in the next pomodoro — verb, deliverable, size — and drag it to
          Done when it is. Saved in your browser between sessions.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a class="card" href="/timer/">
        <span class="num">While you work</span>
        <h3>Session timer</h3>
        <p>
          Three 50-minute blocks with real breaks and a report-back, or the classic 25-on/5-off
          rhythm. Built for the big screen; works offline.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Topics</h2>
      <p>
        Optional. A session runs fine without one, but a short themed discussion is what gets people
        through the door the first time — and it's what turns three hours of silence into something
        people look forward to.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each is a twenty-to-thirty minute read plus something concrete to do. There's no order and no
        thread: take whichever problem is currently yours. The list grows as topics get written.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      {topics.map((t) => <TopicCard topic={t} />)}
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
